WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:01.883
- You see.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.310
When we come into this world,

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.133
you like a domestic animal,

00:00:09.823 --> 00:00:12.403
or an animal going in the wild.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.990
So anything that's born
from an egg is an animal.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.520
Now according to history and our books,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.543
humans are the highest form of an animal.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:27.913
So we say.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.220
But as we come up in life,

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.190
you have babies that was born in a home.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:38.623
Raised with character,
raised with their families.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.620
We went on this topic before
in one of my other interviews,

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.660
but it's the same topic
but a little different.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.600
When we come up into these
homes with our family

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.960
and our character, you wind up not having

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.530
a character of your own because

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.020
you have been put in a position

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.270
where you have to care and absolutely

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.210
had to care for others.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.520
Your brothers, your sisters.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.620
And it wasn't a choice for
you to care for others,

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.820
this is just the human way.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.460
We share the bathroom, we
share the breakfast table.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.030
We have to be considerate of
our mother and our father.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:15.380
So, as you evolve and, like as opposed

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.880
to an animal born in the wild.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:19.410
You get your puppies out there,

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.660
they fend, as they grow they fend,

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.853
like pigeons they fight for their food.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.870
Mom teach you how to hunt,
and then it's on you.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.160
And you know if your brother
got a bigger piece of meat

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:31.993
and you born in the wild,

00:01:31.993 --> 00:01:34.827
you got to, like a wolf,
fight for that meat.

00:01:37.365 --> 00:01:42.365
Education is something that
comes in every form of life.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.730
Take a guy like me.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.610
You have people who went to college

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.710
and had high school degrees,

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.860
as opposed to a guy who's
never been to school

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.380
a day in his life.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:57.010
Never had a phone, he's
computer illiterate.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:00.080
He don't read books, hardly
ever been to a library

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.500
or nothing, no brothers, no
sisters, no wife and kids.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.200
But, to hear this mean speak
and the topics he speak on,

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.271
you would think that he's been educated

00:02:10.271 --> 00:02:15.271
in some of the highest
institutions America has to offer.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.560
But he wasn't.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.730
He grew up in the wild, born in the wild,

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:19.910
grew up in the street.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.050
But the different cultures he lived in

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.320
showed him things and learned him things.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:28.180
Like walking down the street
looking at a store window

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.730
and staring at it until
you knew how to read it,

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.050
until you taught yourself how to read it.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:36.550
So life will evolve for you,
if you give it a chance.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.730
But the problem with most people is,

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.950
that they see so many
things that they want to do

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:44.990
and they want in life,
that they really don't

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.370
give themselves a chance to evolve,

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:50.120
'cause they pushing themselves so hard

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:54.280
to get the car, to go on a
cruise, to see Rome, Paris.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.310
To have the big house with
the family and the kids.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.110
And if these things don't
materialize for them,

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.860
then depression set in.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:06.750
Because you feel you didn't
evolve far enough in life.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.100
Then you start looking
for other things to blame,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.380
like if I hadn't married
my husband too soon,

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.060
if I hadn't had the babies too soon,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.080
if I hadn't listened to
my brother, my mother,

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.940
if I did what I wanted to do.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.750
And these things stress you out.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:23.900
And so by the time you feel
you can get it back on track,

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.370
it has took too many years,

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:28.440
now your pensions and
your retirement funds

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.780
have come in jeopardy,
because you feel like

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.013
you made a lot of wrong decisions.

00:03:34.637 --> 00:03:37.720
When life is not racism,

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.450
and it's not the people that's the enemy.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.430
You are your own enemy,
because you want so much.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:48.320
And you want more than you can pay for.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.010
And when these things don't happen,

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.740
you wanting to blame the world.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.560
People commit suicide, kill their babies,

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.560
throw them in fires.

00:03:58.936 --> 00:04:01.580
They have babies at home and
put 'em in a garbage can.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.440
Abort 'em at home.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:04.410
Everything.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.850
And every species.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.470
We feel we're the highest form of species.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.733
But, if you pay attention to animals,

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:19.230
animals don't sit up and
turn on you and lie to you.

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:25.130
Your dog will die for
you and kill for you.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.700
Without any question.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.600
But your brother who come
up in the house with y'all

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.990
when you get grown, someday
y'all will get angry

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.890
at each other and won't even
speak to you no more in life.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.810
And your own mother
will tell her own child

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.910
to get out the house and never come back.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.410
And the child will steal
from his own mother,

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.090
and go in her purse.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.600
Take his brother's wallet.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.250
And all this for a drug.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.940
Or for a car payment.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.943
For a pair of Jordan shoes.

00:04:52.781 --> 00:04:56.400
And when you see a
crack-head or a heroin-head,

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.550
you have to ask yourself
what kind of head am I?

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:03.080
Because the guy that owns
the Lexus or the Rolls-Royce,

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.800
he gonna go to work everyday
and work hard as he can

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.140
to pay for that Rolls-Royce

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.060
and that mansion out in Beverly Hills,

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.460
and the land he lives on,

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:14.370
and send his children to Harvard or Yale.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.643
Somewhere like that.

00:05:15.643 --> 00:05:18.058
So that they can try to
have a good education.

00:05:18.058 --> 00:05:22.370
In his own kids' mind,
they don't want to do that.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:25.740
Daddy left me $10
million, when will he die?

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:28.430
They look at their own
fathers and mothers,

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.000
and say they too healthy.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.870
They're not dying soon.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:34.220
We can't get the will, the $10 million,

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.228
the estate, the big house.

00:05:36.228 --> 00:05:39.500
In history, I will bring this up,

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.845
as the OJ trial and the
Nicole Simpson trial.

00:05:42.845 --> 00:05:47.050
Bad feud between the two but
he can't let that girl go.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.800
Because he feels he'll
lose everything he got.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.730
So some mutiny have to come into play.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:55.690
It's public news, so there's nothing there

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.468
can be said about that.

00:05:57.468 --> 00:05:58.310
'Cause it's all over the news.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.657
This is just my personal
opinion about that.

00:06:00.657 --> 00:06:02.880
The Menendez brothers.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.670
My parents abused us.

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.950
But they're not here to tell you that now.

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.410
And you killed them.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.890
And then you thought
you was gonna get money,

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.220
but they took them to two trials

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.830
until they broke them,
now as far as I know

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.910
they may be in prison for
the rest of their lives.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.750
Haven't followed up on that.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.403
But over the history of time,

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:23.840
when you say education,
education never stops.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.770
Because every decade, every ten years,

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:30.340
we change, technology change things.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.670
So when you have spent your money

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:34.990
to go to Harvard and Yale in the 60's,

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.870
in the 70's, you will
see that this knowledge

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.790
merely don't count no more.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.630
Because the stuff you learned in the 80's,

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:43.440
you have to re-educate
yourself for the 90's.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.280
And the stuff you learned in the 90's,

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.930
you have to re-educate
yourself for the 2000's.

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:51.070
And who knows what will happen by 2030,

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.410
we might have spaceship cars, flying.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:54.530
I'm 63.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.470
So I don't know that
I'll be here to see that.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.930
But you might have red
lights up in the sky.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.670
And how many tickets
will you give in the sky

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.776
when you got 50000 cars flying,

00:07:03.776 --> 00:07:06.990
passing each other doing 70 miles an hour

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.173
in the big wide open sky?

00:07:08.173 --> 00:07:11.390
They feel that we don't have
to obey a speed limit up here.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.035
And can you put a speed
sign up in mid-air?

00:07:14.035 --> 00:07:17.480
Or will they have to build
some kind of contrapment

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.847
up there to stick poles in the sky

00:07:19.847 --> 00:07:23.340
and say you can only do 35 miles an hour.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.373
Up by this cloud.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:31.080
My point is when you talk about God.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:32.300
See a lot of people when we going God,

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.453
a lot of people thought about religion.

00:07:36.704 --> 00:07:41.704
And we put evil and a good
entity facing each other.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.320
That's not what it's about.

00:07:45.428 --> 00:07:48.910
You see, the war in
heaven was about Lucifer,

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:51.630
which was God's mightiest angels,

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:55.840
and God saying, I'ma give the
people what they want too.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.400
The cars and the houses and all that.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.963
But we don't want them to learn too fast,

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.840
so they'll know how to adapt
to these type of things.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.540
Without hurting each other and
without killing each other.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:08.797
And then when Lucifer argument would be,

00:08:08.797 --> 00:08:11.640
oh, you want to control them.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:16.640
Why not just put it out
there and let them decide.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.603
Because then they'll
be hurting each other,

00:08:19.603 --> 00:08:21.030
like are you sure about that?

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:23.440
Or do you just want
them under your control?

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.853
So then we took it over
and the Bible was made.

00:08:28.178 --> 00:08:29.883
So we took it as evil
fighting a religious thing.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.900
Evil versus positive.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:37.790
Or however you want to say it.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.020
Good and evil.

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:41.092
But it wasn't about that,

00:08:41.092 --> 00:08:43.300
it was like two brothers
come up in the house.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:47.160
One say, well Mom say I want to buy a car,

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.470
but let's get the station wagon.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.983
No, let's get the Camaro over there.

00:08:53.074 --> 00:08:54.490
Well what about the kids?

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.340
Same thing in heaven.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.260
Let's give it to 'em.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.403
Let them handle it.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:02.950
God controls heaven.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.050
I'm the Father.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:05.490
You are just my son.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:08.970
Just like you would go against
your own father in the house.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.200
I'm your dad.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.700
We not gon' do it like this.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.120
Or you're gon' get out of my house.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.650
But we turned it into a war in heaven.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.500
So he kicked him out his house.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.700
You do it your way then.

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:23.780
He was rich, he had power.

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:25.720
He wasn't God but he had power.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:27.460
Had his own money or whatever.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:30.800
Started this thing, what we call evil.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.837
Cars, drugs, money.

00:09:32.837 --> 00:09:34.260
And the people loved it.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:36.770
And when he went to God, his
father, he said they love it.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.620
But yes, but they hurting each other.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.830
And they killing each other behind it.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.323
And so we made it that.

00:09:43.323 --> 00:09:46.550
What we was going to
have all the same things,

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:50.270
just one felt like we
should have took our time,

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:53.883
and got to adapt to
this and learn to this,

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:59.320
'cause he wanted you to
appreciate life for life.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.200
Not appreciate life for
what it can give you.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.390
Or what you could get out of it.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:08.170
Because he knew that
someday you would die,

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.140
and you cannot take any of this with you.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:14.110
And if you live like
that, not appreciating

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:17.220
life for life, and
appreciating life for things,

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.290
then your children will follow that.

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:23.070
Like a man come up drinking in the house,

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:24.360
beating up his wife.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:27.820
His sons will get drunk,
and see his dad doing it.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:28.980
And before you know it, 12 years old,

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.783
they gon' slap a girl, bow!

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:33.990
The first time is hard.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:35.450
Then it gets easier as you drink.

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:36.850
The second time is easier.

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:37.870
The third time is easier.

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:40.110
The problem with me is I
never, ever hit a girl.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:43.560
Called a lot girls bitches,
and sluts, and whores.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:44.550
They ripped me off.

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:47.000
But I could never bring myself to hit one,

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.163
because I knew, once
you crossed that line,

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:52.830
there's no point to return.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:53.940
Like to drink.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.680
I never had to drink in my life.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:58.697
Not because I was better,
because I'm homeless out here

00:10:58.697 --> 00:11:01.590
with everybody else and don't
have a dime in the world.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.190
No brothers no sisters,
again, like I said,

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:04.400
no wife and kids.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:07.430
But I never took one sip of that alcohol.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.623
Because when I saw what it
was doing to my friends,

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:15.520
I did not want myself to turn into that.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.990
I did not hit the crack
pipe, I did not do crystal,

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.823
I did not do heroin, I
did not do powder coke.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:25.260
But I do do a drug, and
it involves marijuana.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.817
Well I don't do this
to make myself better,

00:11:27.817 --> 00:11:31.110
but you will never, ever enjoy life,

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:36.070
until you can learn to relax
and appreciate life for life.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:38.420
Because it has so much to offer,

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.320
and we so busy running for things.

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:42.100
Like you take that GameBoy.

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:43.393
Or that Xbox.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.763
You buy a game for that Xbox,

00:11:46.763 --> 00:11:49.180
and every time you buy a game,

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.480
you got to buy a new machine.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.180
So you have to ask yourself,

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.330
how many kids I got in my family?

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:58.570
And how many machines am I
gonna buy and spoil this person,

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:02.350
before I decide that I'm not
gonna spend another $300.

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:03.500
And you take those Jordans.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.650
Michael Jordan is damn
good basketball player,

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:07.730
and I have nothing against him.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.373
Magic Johnson, all them.

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:13.150
And I love those people on the court.

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:15.420
But we don't even know these people.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.587
And when they die we cry for them,

00:12:16.587 --> 00:12:18.990
and we give them all our money.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.880
Three and four hundred
dollars for a pair of Jordans.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.183
And that's nice if you can afford that

